Rating guidelines: A company that rigorously subjects all AI models and algorithms to independent civil rights and bias audits, obtains explicit consent and compensation for training data, maintains full transparency and human oversight on high-stakes automated decisions, and safeguards youth mental health gets a 100. A company that implements standard baseline AI governance and complies with legal requirements without independent third-party audits gets a 50. A company that deploys discriminatory or exploitative algorithms, scrapes IP and private data without consent, conceals known mental health or algorithmic harms, or uses automated surveillance to penalize workers gets a 1.